==============================================================================================================
V1_density_screen -- one-constant symmetron-type density screen in place of gamma_L / L*
==============================================================================================================

[Part A] sympy: the screen's equations
A1 PASS 0/0/0/0 all 0 :: uniform s: mu_S = 1 - s/(1+x); s=1 -> x/(1+x); s=0 -> 1; on-shell P-sector L_P0 = (a0^2/K)(x - ln(1+x))
A2 PASS 0/0/0 all 0 :: psi EL / v^2 = lap psi - mu^2 psi(psi^2-1) - (rho c^2/M^2) psi + (2/v^2) psi L_P0; v-free at L_P0 = 0; uniform psi^2 = 1 - rho/rho_*
A3 PASS -psi*(psi - psi_a)*(psi + psi_a); 0 psi(psi_a-psi)(psi_a+psi) >= 0; 0 :: exterior u = psi_a - psi subharmonic -> u <= u(R) R/r; then 1 - s/s_a <= 2R/r - R^2/r^2 <= 2R/r
A4 PASS [0]; 0; lim k->oo omega^2 = K*rho_tau*(M - S)/S [0]; 0; K rho_tau (M - S)/S (finite) :: c=0: omega^2 = rho_tau (k^2/chi_S - K), chi_S = S k^2/(K M) + mu_K^2/K; S=1 is H4's gamma_L=0 relation; UV limit finite for S>0
   coupled det (c != 0) is a polynomial of degree 2 in omega^2

